<title>PORTUGAL: BCP unit sets early repayment on 2002 bond.</title>
<headline>BCP unit sets early repayment on 2002 bond.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>BCP Bank &amp; Trust Co (Cayman) Limited, a unit of Banco Comercial Portugues (BCP), on Monday announced the early repayment of its 140 million Ecu convertible bond.</p>
<p>The 8.75 percent guaranteed subordinated convertible bonds were due by 2002 but the bank said it would pay back the total outstanding on May 21, 1997.</p>
<p>Investors have the option to convert their bonds into BCP shares by May 13 at a price of 1,806 escudos.</p>
<p>At 1200 GMT BCP shares were quoted at 2,492 escudos, down 8.0 from Friday's close.</p>
<p>-- Lisbon editorial +(351-1) 3538254</p>
</text>
